   $q$In which pair of sentences is the transition word used incorrectly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"We mixed the blue and yellow paint. Then we painted the box green.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"I love fruit. For example, I eat an apple every day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-example"},{"text":"The park was crowded. However, there were people everywhere.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It was very cold outside. So I wore my warm hat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The park was crowded. However, there were people everywhere.$q$, $q$"However" shows a contrast, but people being everywhere agrees with a crowded park, so the transition is wrong there. The cold weather pair is correct because "So" shows that the cold caused the writer to wear a hat.$q$, 'draft', null)
