   $q$Read the sentences: (A) For example, they turn off the lights when a room is empty. (B) Our school has a team of students called the Energy Helpers. (C) They also check that classroom windows are closed in winter. (D) Because of their work, our school uses less power. Which sentence should come first?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"addition-before-topic"},{"text":"Sentence A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-before-topic"},{"text":"Sentence B","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-as-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence B$q$, $q$Sentence B introduces the Energy Helpers, so it is the topic sentence and must come first. Sentence A starts with "For example," so it needs an idea before it to give an example of.$q$, 'draft', null)
